{"type":"message","id":"d1bda632","parentId":"d283daf2","timestamp":"2026-03-07T04:09:03.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8629116ac5e34d27bec601f4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Next Steps: Task 2.4 - Integration Testing\r\n\r\n**Status**: Ready to Start  \r\n**Estimated Time**: 6-8 hours  \r\n**Target Coverage**: > 80%\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nTask 2.4 is the final task in Priority 2. It involves creating comprehensive tests for all components to ensure everything works together correctly.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## What Needs to Be Done\r\n\r\n### 1. Set Up Test Framework (1-2 hours)\r\n\r\n**Choose test framework**:\r\n- Option A: Jest (recommended for Node.js)\r\n- Option B: Vitest (faster, modern)\r\n\r\n**Install dependencies**:\r\n```bash\r\nnpm install --save-dev jest @types/jest ts-jest\r\n# or\r\nnpm install --save-dev vitest\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Create test configuration**:\r\n- `jest.config.js` or `vitest.config.ts`\r\n- `tsconfig.test.json` (if needed)\r\n- `.testignore` (if needed)\r\n\r\n**Create test directory structure**:\r\n```\r\ntests/\r\n├── unit/\r\n│   ├── database.test.ts\r\n│   ├── errors.test.ts\r\n│   ├── validation.test.ts\r\n│   └── logger.test.ts\r\n├── integration/\r\n│   ├── api.test.ts\r\n│   ├── database.test.ts\r\n│   └── auth.test.ts\r\n└── e2e/\r\n    └── workflow.test.ts\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 2. Unit Tests (2-3 hours)\r\n\r\n#### Database Models Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/unit/database.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- User model CRUD operations\r\n- API key generation and validation\r\n- Agent config storage and retrieval\r\n- Deployment creation and updates\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('UserModel', () => {\r\n  it('should create a user', () => {\r\n    const user = UserModel.create('test@example.com', 'Test User');\r\n    expect(user.email).toBe('test@example.com');\r\n    expect(user.name).toBe('Test User');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should find user by ID', () => {\r\n    const user = UserModel.create('test@example.com', 'Test User');\r\n    const found = UserModel.findById(user.id);\r\n    expect(found).toBeDefined();\r\n    expect(found?.email).toBe('test@example.com');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should update user', () => {\r\n    const user = UserModel.create('test@example.com', 'Test User');\r\n    UserModel.update(user.id, { name: 'Updated User' });\r\n    const updated = UserModel.findById(user.id);\r\n    expect(updated?.name).toBe('Updated User');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should delete user', () => {\r\n    const user = UserModel.create('test@example.com', 'Test User');\r\n    UserModel.delete(user.id);\r\n    const found = UserModel.findById(user.id);\r\n    expect(found).toBeUndefined();\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Error Handling Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/unit/errors.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- Error class instantiation\r\n- Error serialization\r\n- Error type checking\r\n- Error conversion\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('ValidationError', () => {\r\n  it('should create validation error', () => {\r\n    const error = new ValidationError('Invalid input', { field: 'name' });\r\n    expect(error.code).toBe('VALIDATION_ERROR');\r\n    expect(error.statusCode).toBe(400);\r\n    expect(error.message).toBe('Invalid input');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should serialize to JSON', () => {\r\n    const error = new ValidationError('Invalid input', { field: 'name' });\r\n    const json = error.toJSON();\r\n    expect(json.code).toBe('VALIDATION_ERROR');\r\n    expect(json.statusCode).toBe(400);\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Validation Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/unit/validation.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- String validation\r\n- Email validation\r\n- UUID validation\r\n- Enum validation\r\n- Custom validation (soul ID, agent name, etc.)\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('Validation', () => {\r\n  it('should validate required field', () => {\r\n    expect(() => validateRequired('', 'field')).toThrow();\r\n    expect(() => validateRequired('value', 'field')).not.toThrow();\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should validate email', () => {\r\n    expect(() => validateEmail('invalid', 'email')).toThrow();\r\n    expect(() => validateEmail('test@example.com', 'email')).not.toThrow();\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should validate soul ID', () => {\r\n    expect(() => validateSoulId('invalid-soul', 'soulId')).toThrow();\r\n    expect(() => validateSoulId('musk', 'soulId')).not.toThrow();\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Logger Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/unit/logger.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- Logger instantiation\r\n- Log level filtering\r\n- Log file creation\r\n- Log rotation\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 3. Integration Tests (2-3 hours)\r\n\r\n#### API Endpoints Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/integration/api.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- Health check endpoint\r\n- Soul listing endpoint\r\n- Soul retrieval endpoint\r\n- API key validation endpoint\r\n- Agent generation endpoint\r\n- Agent status endpoint\r\n- Agent listing endpoint\r\n- Deployment creation endpoint\r\n- Deployment status endpoint\r\n- Statistics endpoint\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('API Endpoints', () => {\r\n  it('should return health status', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app).get('/api/health');\r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(200);\r\n    expect(response.body.status).toBe('ok');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should list souls', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app).get('/api/v1/souls');\r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(200);\r\n    expect(response.body.success).toBe(true);\r\n    expect(response.body.data).toBeInstanceOf(Array);\r\n    expect(response.body.count).toBe(10);\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should generate agent with valid API key', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'musk', agentName: 'Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(200);\r\n    expect(response.body.success).toBe(true);\r\n    expect(response.body.data.configId).toBeDefined();\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should reject agent generation without API key', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'musk', agentName: 'Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(401);\r\n    expect(response.body.success).toBe(false);\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Database Integration Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/integration/database.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- Database initialization\r\n- Schema creation\r\n- Data persistence\r\n- Transaction handling\r\n- Foreign key constraints\r\n\r\n#### Authentication Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- API key validation\r\n- Key expiration\r\n- Key revocation\r\n- User ownership verification\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 4. End-to-End Tests (1-2 hours)\r\n\r\n#### Complete Workflow Tests\r\n**File**: `tests/e2e/workflow.test.ts`\r\n\r\n**Test scenarios**:\r\n1. Generate agent and check status\r\n2. Generate agent and create deployment\r\n3. List user's agents\r\n4. Check deployment status\r\n5. Error recovery workflow\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('End-to-End Workflow', () => {\r\n  it('should complete full agent generation workflow', async () => {\r\n    // 1. Generate agent\r\n    const genResponse = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'musk', agentName: 'E2E Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(genResponse.status).toBe(200);\r\n    const configId = genResponse.body.data.configId;\r\n\r\n    // 2. Check status\r\n    const statusResponse = await request(app)\r\n      .get(`/api/v1/agents/${configId}/status`)\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123');\r\n    \r\n    expect(statusResponse.status).toBe(200);\r\n    expect(statusResponse.body.data.status).toBe('ready_for_deployment');\r\n\r\n    // 3. Create deployment\r\n    const deployResponse = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/deployments')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ configId, targetSystem: 'openclaw' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(deployResponse.status).toBe(200);\r\n    const deploymentId = deployResponse.body.data.deploymentId;\r\n\r\n    // 4. Check deployment status\r\n    const deployStatusResponse = await request(app)\r\n      .get(`/api/v1/deployments/${deploymentId}`)\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123');\r\n    \r\n    expect(deployStatusResponse.status).toBe(200);\r\n    expect(deployStatusResponse.body.data.status).toBe('pending');\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 5. Error Scenario Tests (1 hour)\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- Missing required fields\r\n- Invalid input values\r\n- Invalid API key\r\n- Unauthorized access\r\n- Resource not found\r\n- Database errors\r\n- Validation errors\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('Error Scenarios', () => {\r\n  it('should return 400 for missing soulId', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ agentName: 'Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(400);\r\n    expect(response.body.error.code).toBe('VALIDATION_ERROR');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should return 401 for invalid API key', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'invalid-key')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'musk', agentName: 'Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(401);\r\n    expect(response.body.error.code).toBe('AUTH_ERROR');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should return 404 for invalid soul', async () => {\r\n    const response = await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'invalid-soul', agentName: 'Test Agent' });\r\n    \r\n    expect(response.status).toBe(404);\r\n    expect(response.body.error.code).toBe('NOT_FOUND');\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 6. Performance Tests (1 hour)\r\n\r\n**Test cases**:\r\n- API response time < 500ms\r\n- Database query time < 100ms\r\n- Concurrent request handling\r\n- Memory usage\r\n\r\n**Example**:\r\n```typescript\r\ndescribe('Performance', () => {\r\n  it('should generate agent in < 500ms', async () => {\r\n    const start = Date.now();\r\n    await request(app)\r\n      .post('/api/v1/agents/generate')\r\n      .set('x-api-key', 'demo-key-123')\r\n      .send({ soulId: 'musk', agentName: 'Perf Test' });\r\n    const duration = Date.now() - start;\r\n    \r\n    expect(duration).toBeLessThan(500);\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('should handle 100 concurrent requests', async () => {\r\n    const promises = [];\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\r\n      promises.push(\r\n        request(app).get('/api/v1/souls')\r\n      );\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    const results = await Promise.all(promises);\r\n    expect(results.every(r => r.status === 200)).toBe(true);\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Test Configuration\r\n\r\n### jest.config.js\r\n```javascript\r\nmodule.exports = {\r\n  preset: 'ts-jest',\r\n  testEnvironment: 'node',\r\n  roots: ['<rootDir>/tests'],\r\n  testMatch: ['**/*.test.ts'],\r\n  collectCoverageFrom: [\r\n    'src/**/*.ts',\r\n    '!src/**/*.d.ts',\r\n  ],\r\n  coverageThreshold: {\r\n    global: {\r\n      branches: 80,\r\n      functions: 80,\r\n      lines: 80,\r\n      statements: 80,\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n### package.json scripts\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"scripts\": {\r\n    \"test\": \"jest\",\r\n    \"test:watch\": \"jest --watch\",\r\n    \"test:coverage\": \"jest --coverage\",\r\n    \"test:unit\": \"jest tests/unit\",\r\n    \"test:integration\": \"jest tests/integration\",\r\n    \"test:e2e\": \"jest tests/e2e\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Coverage Goals\r\n\r\n| Category | Target |\r\n|----------|--------|\r\n| Statements | > 80% |\r\n| Branches | > 80% |\r\n| Functions | > 80% |\r\n| Lines | > 80% |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Timeline\r\n\r\n| Phase | Hours | Status |\r\n|-------|-------|--------|\r\n| Setup | 1-2 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| Unit Tests | 2-3 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| Integration Tests | 2-3 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| E2E Tests | 1-2 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| Error Tests | 1 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| Performance Tests | 1 | ⏳ TODO |\r\n| **Total** | **6-8** | **⏳ TODO** |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Success Criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] All unit tests pass\r\n- [ ] All integration tests pass\r\n- [ ] All E2E tests pass\r\n- [ ] Code coverage > 80%\r\n- [ ] No flaky tests\r\n- [ ] Performance tests pass\r\n- [ ] Error scenarios covered\r\n- [ ] Documentation complete\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## After Task 2.4\r\n\r\nOnce Task 2.4 is complete:\r\n1. Priority 2 will be 100% complete\r\n2. Ready to start Priority 3\r\n3. System will be fully tested and production-ready\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Resources\r\n\r\n### Testing Libraries\r\n- Jest: https://jestjs.io/\r\n- Vitest: https://vitest.dev/\r\n- Supertest: https://github.com/visionmedia/supertest\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n- Jest Testing Guide\r\n- Express Testing Best Practices\r\n- Database Testing Patterns\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Ready to Start**: Yes  \r\n**Estimated Duration**: 6-8 hours  \r\n**Target Coverage**: > 80%  \r\n**Next Phase**: Priority 3 - Advanced Features\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Last Updated**: March 7, 2026\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772856543653}}
